  "number": 5978,
  "title": "Fix type errors in the published typings with skipLibCheck turned off",
  "body": "> TypeScript projects that type-check our published typings (`skipLibCheck: false`) get up to 19 errors from Web Chat's own declarations.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed type errors in the published typings when `skipLibCheck` is turned off, in PR [#5978](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/5978), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe typings had type-only members emitted as values in namespaces, a self-referencing `renderMarkdown.createStreamingRenderer`, non-DOM globals, and 2 constraints failing under `strict`. JavaScript output only changes by the renamed function.\n\n## Design\n\n- Types leave the `export * as` namespaces instead of getting local aliases: they never worked as types there; entry points still export them.\n- Non-DOM globals resolve through `globalThis`, instead of adding `@types/dom-speech-recognition` and `@types/node` to `dependencies`.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `bundle/src/boot`: types exported by `exports/*.ts`, not `actual/*`\n- `renderMarkdown.ts`, `createMarkdownStreamingRenderer.ts`: file and function renamed to `createMarkdownStreamingRenderer`\n- `WebSpeechPonyfill.ts`, `GlobalScopeClock.ts`: globals via new base `TypeOfGlobal`\n- `templateDecorator.tsx`, component `ContextOf.ts`: constraints no longer invariant\n- No new test: each package alone, React 16/18 types: 0 errors from our declarations (React 19: `prop-types` TS7016, fixed by #5973)\n- Not fixed (dependencies): `NetworkInformation` (`botframework-directlinejs`), `Buffer` (`@types/node@10` via `botframework-streaming`), `type-fest` (undeclared by `react-chain-of-responsibility`)\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [ ] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [ ] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
